The hardest part of this lab was that there are so many different tools to
configure and work with that many of the failures and bugs were in figuring
out the right way to use certain tools. My first deployment crashed because
Kubernetes args replace a Dockerfile CMD entirely, so the container tried to
run "--batch-size=50". Switching to ENTRYPOINT instead of CMD fixed it. Pushing
to the registry failed with a 401 even after a successful login, which turned
out to be the Docker CLI looking for credentials in the wrong home directory.
I also spent a while confirming that the lopsided 3-1 and 7-1 splits in Grafana 
were probabilistically possible, rather than a bug, since kube-proxy picks a
backend independently per connection.
